-The most consistent pattern in Table~\ref{tab:results} is that profile type is determined primarily by the domain, not by the model class. All five models classify as \textsc{sustained} or \textsc{delayed\_contiguous} on both PM$_{10}$ stations (10/10 combinations), and all five (plus ARIMA) are \textsc{fragmented} on traffic (6/6). In wind, all models achieve $H^*(\mathrm{relax})=48$ and $H^*(\mathrm{strict})\geq 47$, spanning only \textsc{sustained} and near-sustained \textsc{fragmented} profiles. PM$_{2.5}$ is the only domain where profile type varies across models (Ridge and MLP are \textsc{delayed\_contiguous} or \textsc{fragmented} with long strict intervals, while KNN and LightGBM show shorter strict windows), but even there the overall morphology—delayed onset with eventual positive skill—is shared.
