 \subsection{Electric load as a diagnostic boundary case}
 
-The electric load domain illustrates a qualitatively distinct failure mode and exposes a diagnostic boundary of the framework. Ridge achieves \textsc{sustained} classification with $H^*(\mathrm{strict})=7$ across the full evaluated range $h=1$--7, yet 0\% of horizons are DM-significant after BH correction. This is not a contradiction but a consequence of limited statistical power: across $n\approx 281$ rolling origins, the maximum observed skill is 0.061 (at $h=5$), the minimum detectable effect at 80\% power given this sample size is approximately 0.061, and 90\% bootstrap confidence intervals include zero at all seven horizons.
