-This diagnostic is informative in two directions. First, it demonstrates that $H^*(\mathrm{strict})$ can be positive while DM significance is unattainable, alerting practitioners that the descriptor should be accompanied by sample-size context when evaluation windows are short. Second, it distinguishes the Ridge outcome from the remaining models on this domain: LightGBM and ExtraTrees are \textsc{immediate\_collapse} with 0\% DM significance (negative skill without statistical verification), while KNN and MLP are also \textsc{immediate\_collapse} but with 100\% DM significance in the \emph{wrong direction}—they are significantly worse than persistence. MLP additionally exhibits numerical instability on this domain due to unscaled MW-range target values (the target was deliberately left unscaled as part of the fixed protocol), yielding skill values from $-16$ to $-38$.
